INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal="Locate single-month volume anomalies in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by computing each region×product-line's monthly sales as a multiple of its own 24-month mean, report the top-3 combinations with their multiples, corresponding-month return rates, and assess whether each spike is real demand or channel stuffing. Output a Markdown report saved to disk with inline source annotations, a data table, and a conclusion paragraph."):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max of the month column), and print first 5 rows as sample → db_agent
2. Compute monthly volume ratio per region×product: Using the CSV, for each (region, product_line) group compute the 24-month rolling mean of monthly sales volume, then compute the ratio = current_month_volume / 24-month_mean for every month. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/volume_ratio_analysis.csv) → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 anomalies & fetch return rates: From the ratio CSV, find the top-3 (region, product_line, month) combinations with the highest volume ratio. For each, also extract the return rate (退货率) for that specific month from the original CSV. Save a small summary table to offline_data/top3_anomalies.csv → code_agent
4. Assess demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) the 3-month average volume BEFORE the spike month, (b) the 3-month average volume AFTER the spike month, (c) the return rate trend (spike month vs surrounding months). Save these diagnostic metrics to offline_data/anomaly_diagnostics.csv → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded data: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/volume_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing the top-3 anomalies with ratio, month, return rate; (3) every key number must carry an inline source annotation in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike is more likely real demand or channel stuffing, with reasoning; (5) all data sourced exclusively from the local CSV, no web data. → code_agent
